scores.critique:
It depends on the owner supplying byte-exact headers from a paused lane. Their provenance has documented audit gaps. Model-agnosticism is unconfirmed: SCALED_MODEL_PARAMETERS comes from their header.

At N=64 it puts a foreign engine inside the derivative trust boundary, so a bug there would be correlated across both pipelines. That removes independence exactly where it matters most.

Design A already supplies an in-house sparse engine that is validated against stock CAPD and runs faster per step (about 331 s against 1241 s). The generic CAPD fallback at N=32 needs about 6 GB on a shared machine that already has about 5 GB in use.

Several ideas are worth keeping and folding into A:
- the exact dyadic linear-cell fixture, which tests containment independently of CAPD's DAG;
- the mutation controls;
- writing the full interval M to disk, so radii can be retuned without another C1 run;
- folding the period gate into the C1 run;
- reordering frame.py's Schur form (fast block first), so slow rows do not see fast columns;
- the plain-box MPFR centre, which is a simpler alternative to A's majorant centre (comparable growth, e^{17.8 t}).

designs.result_strength:
If the runs pass, the theorem is the same as at N=8 and N=16, independently re-proved there and new at N = 32 and 64. For Erhardt's 18-state K_i-clamped smoothed TP06 endocardial ring of N cells with coupling c = N^2/64000 per ms (G_Ks = 0.0275, decimals as written):
- there is a rotating-wave periodic orbit x_j(t) = phi(t + jT/N);
- its period lies in an explicit interval (N x the section-time enclosure), and the section point is unique in the stated block-norm ball on {V_0 = s};
- every eigenvalue of the shift-reduced section map Dg has modulus at most q < 1;
- so every nontrivial Floquet multiplier of the full orbit has modulus at most q^N < 1, against all perturbations (the section is the full 18N-1 dimensional one, not a symmetric subspace);
- the orbit is therefore locally orbitally asymptotically stable.
Proving that it is the solution continued from the Hopf branch remains numerical identification, as now. The pipeline is independent of the Mac pipeline in its coefficient algorithm (Jacobian-jet factorization, not DAG pruning) and in its centre method. It shares CAPD's Lohner sets and Poincaré map as trusted library code. N=32 is very likely within reach (margin about 1e-5, about 20 to 30 min per pass). N=64 is feasible in time and memory (about 1 to 1.5 h, about 4 GB) but conditional on the Dg width budget.
